<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Trinitaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1838–1844</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as The Trinitarians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">La Trinitaria was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/secret-society">secret society</a> founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a> on 16 July 1838 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-pablo-duarte">Juan Pablo Duarte</a> and his companions to free the eastern part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a> from Haitian rule. Its members, organised in cells of three, spread the cause of a sovereign <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a> under the motto Dios, Patria, Libertad. Its leaders proclaimed independence on 27 February 1844, though Duarte was soon sidelined by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-santana">Pedro Santana</a>.</p></div>
